From: Valera Kozlov <valera.kozlov19@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 02:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: add MT7988 WO2 firmware support

mtk_wed_mcu_load_firmware() only distinguished two cases for MT7988
(wo->hw->index ? WO1 : WO0), silently loading WO1 for any index > 0,
including index 2 (the third WED unit, reachable on boards where hif2
sits on PCI domain 2 -- see companion patch
999-wed-mtk_wed-refactor-attach-for-support-wed2.patch). No WO2
firmware file exists in linux-firmware or the mtk-openwrt-feeds vendor
feed for this platform.

Add an explicit MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO2 define and a proper switch over
wo->hw->index so index 2 loads its own firmware file instead of
silently reusing WO1's.

The firmware binary itself (mt7988_wo_2.bin) was extracted from the
official ASUS ZenWiFi BT8 factory firmware (v3.0.0.6.102_58407) and
is packaged separately via package/firmware/linux-firmware. WO0 and
WO1 in that same factory firmware are byte-for-byte identical (MD5)
to the upstream linux-firmware mt7988_wo_0.bin/mt7988_wo_1.bin,
confirming WO2 is sourced from the same official MediaTek SDK release
rather than a device-specific or incompatible build.

Verified on ASUS ZenWiFi BT8 (MT7988D): with this patch and the
companion attach-path fix, wed device 2 attaches successfully and the
router operates normally with wed_enable=1 persisted across reboots.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_wo.h	2026-08-23 13:13:10.615864219 +0300
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_wo.h	2026-08-22 02:58:32.618429428 +0300
@@ -93,6 +93,7 @@
 #define MT7986_FIRMWARE_WO1	"mediatek/mt7986_wo_1.bin"
 #define MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO0	"mediatek/mt7988/mt7988_wo_0.bin"
 #define MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO1	"mediatek/mt7988/mt7988_wo_1.bin"
+#define MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO2	"mediatek/mt7988/mt7988_wo_2.bin"
 
 #define MTK_WO_MCU_CFG_LS_BASE				0
 #define MTK_WO_MCU_CFG_LS_HW_VER_ADDR			(MTK_WO_MCU_CFG_LS_BASE + 0x000)
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_mcu.c	2026-08-23 13:13:10.616794761 +0300
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_mcu.c	2026-08-22 02:58:32.619524928 +0300
@@ -390,8 +390,19 @@
 						: MT7986_FIRMWARE_WO0;
 		break;
 	case 3:
-		fw_name = wo->hw->index ? MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO1
-					: MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO0;
+		switch (wo->hw->index) {
+		case 0:
+			fw_name = MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO0;
+			break;
+		case 1:
+			fw_name = MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO1;
+			break;
+		case 2:
+			fw_name = MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO2;
+			break;
+		default:
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -464,3 +475,4 @@
 MODULE_FIRMWARE(MT7986_FIRMWARE_WO1);
 MODULE_FIRMWARE(MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO0);
 MODULE_FIRMWARE(MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO1);
+MODULE_FIRMWARE(MT7988_FIRMWARE_WO2);
